live-draw: zeta reads as textures: snapshot grows with the largest clip, depth formats prefer the zeta over a colour
surface at the same address, a draw that does not write depth reads its own zeta's snapshot; LD_ZPROBE diagnostic.

Symptom (Killzone 3, rounds 22-23): in the first level the depth-of-field inputs were flat (the 320x180 F_X32
DepthToFuzzy target 0x1A1C000 one value, 4.88e-5 = every depth read 0) and the deferred lighting read depth 0.

Cause 1: the R32F snapshot of a zeta was sized from the clip of the first pass that bound it. KZ3 first binds its
1280x720 Z24S8 scene zeta (0x25C0000) with a 512x512 clip, so the snapshot stayed 512x512 and later 1280x720 reads
(half-res depth downsample, lighting, DoF) got 0 outside the top-left corner. The snapshot now grows to the largest
clip bound since (LD_NO_ZSNAP_GROW=1 = old).
Cause 2: 0x2980000 is both the shadow map's colour target and a zeta; its X16 / DEPTH16 reads matched the colour
surface first (zeros). A depth-format read at an address with a written host zeta now binds the zeta snapshot
(LD_NO_ZETA_PREFER=1 = old).
Cause 3: a draw that samples the zeta it has bound fell back to guest VRAM (never written). With depth write off
(KZ3 deferred lighting, soft particles) it now reads the snapshot, as RSX does (LD_NO_ZSELF_SNAP=1 = old).
Diagnostic: LD_ZPROBE=<n> [LD_ZPROBE_GATE=<file>] logs, once per (shader control, colour target) per frame, which
resource each zeta-aliased unit got and three texels of the snapshot and guest VRAM, and the zeta a depth-export
draw wrote. Off by default.

Verified: tools/smoke/test_zeta_reads.c (Proton) PASS 256/256; each LD_NO_* control FAILs.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.15.0 (SPU pass 81): partly absorbed, PR280 depth textures, our zeta-alias kinds, switches and probe kept over it.
Pass 83: v0.15.0 has zdepth_grow_snapshot itself (from our PR 280); this patch only adds the LD_NO_ZSNAP_GROW
switch to it (pass 81 had added a second copy: redefinition, the Windows build failed).

diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c b/libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c
--- a/libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c
@@ -4372,7 +4372,10 @@ static D3D12_CPU_DESCRIPTOR_HANDLE dsv_handle(u32 slot)
